  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. The issue was in the `removeMember` function at line 94, where it was calling `assertLastOwnerRetained` with `\"owner\"` as the nextRole parameter. \n\nThe `assertLastOwnerRetained` function returns early if `nextRole === \"owner\"` (since promoting someone to owner doesn't cause the org to lose an owner), which bypassed the validation entirely. \n\nBy changing it to pass `\"admin\"` instead, the validation now runs correctly and prevents removal of the last owner—since removal is effectively a demotion to no role, as stated in the code comment. The fix ensures that:\n\n1. Attempting to demote the last owner is correctly refused ✓\n2. Attempting to remove the last owner is now correctly refused ✓\n3. All 617 tests pass ✓",
